## When TestSprite finishes (or any `test initiate` / MCP test run)

1. Read the TestSprite report / pass-fail matrix (e.g. `testsprite_tests/testsprite-mcp-test-report.md` or MCP dashboard result).
2. For **each failing check** (not warnings-only / flakes you already closed):
   - Deduplicate: search open cards on this board for the same TC id or title before creating.
   - Create a card on **Reported** (`add_card_to_list`) with:
     - **Name:** `[TestSprite] <TC id or check name> — <short symptom>`
     - **Description** (markdown):
       - Surface / URL under test (prefer `http://127.0.0.1:4175/...` or cockpit `.../spec-ops?screen=...`)
       - Expected vs actual
       - Environment (**sandbox** Supabase ref `glpdpkozvmfzgoewquxi` for local QA; never claim prod unless that was the target)
       - Evidence: report path, screenshot path, TestSprite run link if available
       - `gitSha` / `build-meta.json` when local preview was used
3. Summarize in chat: N cards filed + Trello board link. Do not only paste a fail matrix without filing.

## Lifecycle (agent moves cards; owner confirms Done)

| Event | List |
|---|---|
| New TestSprite / manual bug | → **Reported** |
| Starting fix | → **In Progress** |
| Fix in local preview / ready to recheck | → **Confirm Fix** + comment with SHA + preview URL |
| Owner/QA confirms | → **Done** (do **not** auto-Done) |
| Cannot reproduce on retest | → **Can't reproduce** + comment with evidence |

## Rules

- Prefer **Trello** for product bugs found by TestSprite or exploratory QA. Keep Linear/`npm run qa-result` for the existing Linear QA-pass workflow when that is what the user asked for — do not replace Linear silently.
- One failing TestSprite case → one card (unless the user asks to batch).
- Attach screenshots via Trello MCP when available; otherwise link file paths in the description.
- Never put secrets (API keys, tokens, `.env`, passwords) on cards.
- Template/example cards must not be recreated; the board starts clean of Bug-tracker template copy.
- Local TestSprite runs must use **sandbox** data only; do not point local `.env` at production for this routine.

## Quick agent checklist

- [ ] `.env` = sandbox; `deploy:local` on 4175; `build-meta.json` matches SHA
- [ ] TestSprite run finished against local preview
- [ ] Active board = Mings Bug Tracker
- [ ] Failures filed to **Reported** (or updated if duplicate)
- [ ] Chat names the cards / counts filed
- [ ] Fix path updates list + comments; Done only after human confirm
